From wayne_betws at hotmail.com  Tue Nov 17 10:37:48 2009
From: wayne_betws at hotmail.com (wayne jones)
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2009 10:37:48 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rpy] suppress R warnings with RPy2
In-Reply-To: <4B027F03.6050802@gmail.com>
References: <4B027F03.6050802@gmail.com>
Message-ID: <BAY131-W29E3FE0F3A0E910D1055E083A40@phx.gbl>


 

See "help(warning)" in R.

 

To completely suppress warnings do: 

>options(warn=-1)


 

Also see help(suppressWarnings) in R which may be more appropriate if you know where the warnings originate from. 

 

> suppressWarnings(for(i in 1:3) {m <- matrix(1:7, 3,4) })
> for(i in 1:3) {m <- matrix(1:7, 3,4) }


 

Regards, 

Wayne

 


 
